claim.claim-text:
a differential assembly (32) that has a ring gear (72) and is rotatable about a first axis (60);
a drive pinion (36) that meshes with the ring gear (72) and is rotatable about a second axis (90);
a first electric motor (38) that is selectively connectable to the drive pinion (36) via a first gear set (42); and
a second electric motor (40) that is selectively connectable to the drive pinion (36) via a second gear set (44) that is spaced apart from the first gear set (42), wherein the first gear set (42) has a different gear ratio than the second gear set (44).

the first gear set (42) has a first gear (130) that is coupled to the first electric motor (38) and is rotatable about the first motor axis (110), and a second gear (132) that is selectively couplable to the drive pinion (36) with a first clutch (150);
the second electric motor (40) is rotatable about a second motor axis (120); and
the second gear set (44) has a third gear (140) that is coupled to the second electric motor (40) and is rotatable about the second motor axis (120), and a fourth gear (142) that is selectively couplable to the drive pinion (36) with a second clutch (152).

a first differential assembly (32) that is rotatable about a first differential axis (310);
a second differential assembly (32') that is rotatable about a second differential axis (310');
a first electric motor (38) that is operatively connectable to the first differential assembly (32); and
a second electric motor (40) that is operatively connectable to the second differential assembly (32'), wherein the first electric motor (38) and the second electric motor (40) are operatively connectable in series with a clutch (300).
